<%= header_section("Finance report backstop aborted") %>
<div>
  <p>The daily backstop (<code>VerifyFinanceReportsDeliveryJob</code>) refused to treat completion keys as missing because a Redis write/read probe failed. Re-enqueueing on a lying GET would produce a burst of false alerts.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Reason: <code><%= @reason %></code></li>
    <li>Apparent misses: <%= @miss_count %></li>
    <li>Job classes: <%= @class_names.presence&.join(", ") || "(none)" %></li>
  </ul>
  <p>Nothing was re-enqueued. If a specific report is actually missing, re-run that job with pinned period args rather than waiting for the next backstop tick.</p>
</div>
